{"seq":48,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24964"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish-mge card ppm-128, category 1; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Earth Science] What is the difference between lava and magma?\nA. Magma contains more gas and is less viscous than lava\nB. There is no difference\nC. Whether they are found inside the Earth or not\nAnswer: C. Magma and lava are essentially the same substance — molten rock — but they are called different names based on their location. Magma is the term used when this molten rock is beneath the Earth’s surface. When magma erupts from a volcano and flows over the land or seabed, it’s known as lava.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/mythology, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, earth-space/a","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish-mge/ppm-128.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"Molten rock beneath the Earth's surface is magma — what is it called once it erupts onto the surface?"},{"field":"de","new":"Geschmolzenes Gestein unter der Erdoberfläche heißt Magma – wie nennt man es, sobald es an die Oberfläche ausbricht?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish-mge","card":"ppm-128","category":1}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Earth Science] What is the difference between lava and magma?\nA. Magma contains more gas and is less viscous than lava\nB. There is no difference\nC. Whether they are found inside the Earth or not\nAnswer: C. Magma and lava are essentially the same substance — molten rock — but they are called different names based on their location. Magma is the term used when this molten rock is beneath the Earth’s surface. When magma erupts from a volcano and flows over the land or seabed, it’s known as lava."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f10934"}],"hash":"b2800a7716c5"},
